covariant-derivative-of-christoffel-symb.limits_and_boundary:
In locally inertial coordinates (Riemann normal coordinates) centered at a spacetime point $P$, $\Gamma^ho_{
u\sigma}(P) = 0$, but the derivative $\partial_\mu \Gamma^ho_{
u\sigma}(P)$ generally remains non-zero in curved spacetime, directly determining the Riemann curvature tensor at $P$. In globally flat Minkowski spacetime with Cartesian coordinates, $\partial_\mu \Gamma^ho_{
u\sigma} = 0$ everywhere.
